# What this repo is for: the workbench TOOLCHAIN — the build, sync, probe and
# retention scripts, their configs, and the written protocols/results that
# explain them. Everything a script PRODUCES stays out, however valuable it is
# to have on disk.
#
# The rule of thumb when adding to this file: if deleting it would only cost a
# re-run, ignore it. If deleting it would lose a decision or a method, track it.

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Derived data, one timestamped tree per build; prune-build-products.sh owns
# its retention. 12G at the time this repo was created.
build-products/

# Runtime device locks: build-install-iphone.sh serialises install+launch per
# UDID here. Pure runtime state — deleting one only costs a re-run.
locks/

# Git worktrees belonging to OTHER repositories. Tracking these would nest
# repos inside this one.
worktrees/

# ── Large binaries and third-party tooling ──────────────────────────────────
whisper-models/
gltf-tools/
prelogin-assets-compressed/
landmark-refs/
backups/

# ── Generated evidence and captures ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The soak PROTOCOL, verdicts and written results ARE tracked (they carry the
# method and the conclusions); only the raw per-run capture stream is not.
thermal-soak/raw/
evidence/
visualizations/
artifact-workbench/
recycling-bin/items/

# ── Logs, traces, runtime state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.pid
*.trace
gcl-sync-state.json
gcl-downstream-sync-state.json

# ── Editor / OS / backup noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.bak
*.bak-*
node_modules/

# Probe run-state, regenerable by re-running the probe that writes it.
# thermal-subscreen-state.json says so in its own note ("Delete this file to
# force a full re-measurement"), and a03-last-regression.txt is one run's
# stdout. Tracked at import by oversight; they only ever churn.
a03-last-regression.txt
thermal-subscreen-state.json
